  "description": "Delicately sweet with a hint of bitterness, swapping out store-bought chocolate liqueur with this homemade version made with cacao nibs is like adding expensive dark chocolate to your drink instead of a jigger of Nestle Quik.",
  "notes": "Total time, including resting: 9 days 10 min.\n\nNotes: Cacao nibs are pieces of cacao beans that have been roasted. Many grocery and health-food stores carry them, but if yours doesn't, you can order them from a variety of online sources.\n\nMake-ahead and storage: Refrigeration isn't necessary; the liqueur should keep for about two months.",
